{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1410130-astral-space-in-scion","id":1410130,"title":"Astral Space in Scion?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-24T14:27:34-07:00","id":1410130,"title":"Astral Space in Scion?","content":"I was great fan of <b>Mage: The Awakening</b>. In <b>Scion</b> I have most of what I loved about <b>MtAw</b> - powerful magic, mythological stories, otherworld realms - and with <b>Companion</b>, even Atlantis is here. In <b>MtAw </b>I loved also one more element - dream realms of Astral Space, connecting whole humanity. From my read of <b>Scion 2E Origin</b> and <b>Hero</b> I do not see realms as Astral - but maybe I missed something? If not, how do you think I could insert Astral in <b>Scion</b>? Common Otherworld for Gods and mythical beings, created by dreams of humans, that let some of mythics to enter it?<br /> <br /> EDIT: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15464-raphatheascended\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar15464_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"15464\" data-vbnamecard=\"15464\">RaphaTheAscended</a> found the solution - <i>Aether</i> Realm, from <b>Scion</b> 2E <b>Origin</b> book. Here is quote about it:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Origin, p. 37</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Aether:</b> Greek, Indian, and modern occult sources have written extensively about the Aether, and have given it other names, such as Indra\u2019s Net and the Astral Plane. The Aether is composed of the fifth, subtle element that creates space and distance. Platonists believe that it transmits the \u201clight\u201d of ideal objects which in turn, create the substance of other realms. Mortals have long used techniques to send their souls into the Aether, where they can rise to contemplate The World and Overworld, and Scions may use the same techniques. Ordeals in the Aether take the form of riddles, enigmas, and acts of deep self-realization, administered by the abstract beings who dwell there. Unfortunately, it\u2019s impossible to physically traverse the Aether except with the use of obscure magical powers, and exceedingly difficult to use it to travel to the Underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-25-2020, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T14:46:43-07:00","id":1410132,"title":"","content":"Astral (or something close to it) exists in Scion, but it is related to the myths. The problem is, most of the myths don\u2019t have a classic Astral space as the ones we see in D&amp;D or Mage (both), and usually this kind of place is out of Hero reach, probably closer to a underworld or the place where the gods themselves (Or their enemies) live. The one that came to my mind is the Dream Land from the Mythos, that Probably would be in the reach of heroic.<br /> <br /> We may see something in Demigod, as they will explore some Terrae Incognitae and the Underworlds. For a more (really) astral thing, probably just in God.<br /> <br /> My suggestion is check God 1e, there is something about the overworlds, Titans and the lands of the gods that may interest you as they are less mythic and more RPG stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T19:30:24-07:00","id":1410192,"title":"","content":"I would strongly advise against inserting any idea of Astral Space, as you've described it, into Scion.<br /> <br /> First, because Scion is not part of the rest of the world of OPP games, nor is it meant to be. It can be global in scope and has the potential to include every element that every culture from the beginning of recorded history knows, so... why throw in things that aren't already covered? There are other games for that. It's okay to look at a game and say, &quot;This one doesn't include what I want to play, so I'm going to play another one.&quot; It's not like it was forty years ago when there were only a few games to play and everyone had to fit all of their stories into those rules.<br /> <br /> Second, and more importantly: when you propose a concept like Astral Space that emerges from one culture and decide that it's universal, you're making a delibrate move to erase the uniqueness of other cultures. There is nothing in Scion that is universal. As the game develops, it becomes more and more clear that certain concepts are culturally bound, and the writers for the game try to pay attention to that fact. If you throw in something that erases the distinctions that people make (for good reason), you may need to take a moment to think about why it's important to you to do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T19:53:35-07:00","id":1410197,"title":"","content":"I need to point a few things, while I agree Scion have a more respectful relation to the several cultures shown in the book. There is space for an astral plane in Scion the same way there is space for the Veil (check the Demigod Actual play from OPP con).<br /> <br /> You can have an Astral plane that connect the several god realms or even the underworlds, it can be the gap that Byfrost cross (it has a name with many consonants), the chaos below Tartarus, or the sky beyond the paths of the sun and the moon. It is not breaking the game or disrespecting the cultures more than saying that all the gods are real (not only the ones of the culture pantheon) or that the Deva have a diplomatic relationship with the Aesir (no culture believes that, still it is not disrespectful thing).<br /> <br /> The point is, the way Scion works, this kind of place is beyond the regular access of Heroes and even Demigods, as it\u2019s beyond the reach of physical bodies. Of course there is a dream like dimension where you can enter to reach people dream (Darkeness purview can access, for example), how it work I don\u2019t know, there are explanations for that in each pantheon view, but for a more Astral (in the Mage/D&amp;D use of the word), you probably will have to wait for God and their non physical aspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T20:18:35-07:00","id":1410204,"title":"","content":"Hm i think its a mistake to try and make it a Grand Unified Theory, that applies to everything.<br /> <br /> But that said, it would certainly be interestinf to research which mythologies have &quot;realm of pure thoughts&quot; in their stuff.<br /> Depending on how you classify philosophers theories in scion there might be a case for a theoi aspected midrealm of platonic ideals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T21:15:52-07:00","id":1410214,"title":"","content":"We've got an (officially unofficial) Atlantis Pantheon, right? One that's essentially made up or of whole cloth. Not everything in Scion has to be deeply rooted in real-world mythologies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-25-2020, 12:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T22:07:15-07:00","id":1410221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1410130-astral-space-in-scion?p=1410197#post1410197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is space for an astral plane in Scion the same way there is space for the Veil (check the Demigod Actual play from OPP con).</div> </div> </div> </div>Will watch it, but I suspect the Veil is like the Underworld in WoD / CoD - i.e. cross realm of dead from where they go to their proper afterlife realms?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1410130-astral-space-in-scion?p=1410204#post1410204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that said, it would certainly be interestinf to research which mythologies have &quot;realm of pure thoughts&quot; in their stuff.<br /> Depending on how you classify philosophers theories in scion there might be a case for a theoi aspected midrealm of platonic ideals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are not hindu Deva having their own Dream Domains, also? With reality being Maya and all that? Adding those two with Platonic Ideas realm of Theoi - and you have basis for Astral. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T23:09:18-07:00","id":1410235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1410130-astral-space-in-scion?p=1410221#post1410221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will watch it, but I suspect the Veil is like the Underworld in WoD / CoD - i.e. cross realm of dead from where they go to their proper afterlife realms?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly, it\u2019s more like an cross pantheon afterlife where they agree to let worthy people that would not end on any of the other pantheon afterlife stay. Almost as a Christian heaven or something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T23:52:19-07:00","id":1410237,"title":"","content":"Wyrd if you want to play Mage, you can play Mage, you don't gotta come in here and go &quot;Okay but how do I make Scion into Mage?&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't go into the WoD threads and piss and moan about the mythic inaccuracies of all of the various splats, because then I'd be the asshole and people would quite rightly go &quot;Buddy fuck off and go back to Scion if you like Scion so much&quot;<br /> <br /> Edit: Some Cosmologies have Overworlds, and they're a thousand times more interesting than how I've heard these Astral Realms described. I recommend just using THOSE, because they'll inevitably make for a better story than trying to take something from a different game line and trying to beat it into shape to fit a different line, tone, and setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T23:56:31-07:00","id":1410239,"title":"","content":"If you want to have a crossover between Scion and Mage, just do a full on conversion project, since Mage\u2019s astral space is tied to a number of other aspects of Mage\u2019s cosmology. And actually I\u2019d kinda like such a project, although it should probably best wait until Saints&amp;Monsters come out which give the full rules of how to design Sorcerers which could be modified to make Mages. But if you do want an conversion, then the first thing to recognize is that well, it will still be one cosmology among many, just as true as all others but not more so except to the members or aspects of that cosmology","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24769,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","user":"Magicjohnny","date":". 08-25-2020, 02:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T01:02:05-07:00","id":1410243,"title":"","content":"No, <b>I</b> <b>just want idea of 'Dream Realms'</b> in Scion. It's not the proper crossover, it's <b><i>maybe</i> </b>extra setting element. ( But seeing as idea of Theoi or Deva could have those, it would be enough for me. ) As I pointed above, all other things interesting from Mage are<i> already</i> in Scion. Beside simple 'Dream Realms'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-25-2020, 07:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T03:08:08-07:00","id":1410257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1410130-astral-space-in-scion?p=1410237#post1410237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wyrd if you want to play Mage, you can play Mage, you don't gotta come in here and go &quot;Okay but how do I make Scion into Mage?&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't go into the WoD threads and piss and moan about the mythic inaccuracies of all of the various splats, because then I'd be the asshole and people would quite rightly go &quot;Buddy fuck off and go back to Scion if you like Scion so much&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">If you have a problem with a poster then the report button is right there. This is circuitously cussing someone out.<br /> <br /> Also, if someone wants to combine games, plenty of awesome ones have been done.<br /> <br /> I've played Batman/Vampire The Masquerade for example.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-25-2020, 08:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T04:33:21-07:00","id":1410266,"title":"","content":"I guess what <i>can</i> be taken away from Kyman's comment is that the best way to incorporate a concept into Scion is always to look at what mythological concepts it is similar to. I don't remember whether it was Kyman himself or Samudra who once said it, but essentially, the source material for Scion is the entire 5,000 year corpus of world mythology. There are no truly new ideas when you are working with a source base this large, and games like MtA or VtM or whatever else obviously already draw on this corpus for inspiration. It is easier to incroporate new concepts into Scion once one has related them to what Scion is principally about, namely not fictional mages or fictional werewolves or fictional aliens, but real-world mythology. That is what the game system is derived from and built for, and once one thinks in terms of mythology, one will find it way easier to work with what Scion offers.There are various beliefs and concepts regarding dreams all over the world, from dreams being visitors from the Underworld in Greek epic to dreams being visions of one's nahualli in Mexico. I'm sure you can find something to build on to get your beloved Astral Realms, or at least something functionally similar, into Scion, wyrd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T05:13:10-07:00","id":1410268,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> here a piece of Companion, Atlantean Pantheon Cosmology:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Example: Atlantis lacks an Overworld but possesses an Underworld of sorts: the Void of unshaped chaos where souls go after death. That Underworld holds innumerable Midrealms for those souls to wash ashore if they\u2019re lucky; if not, they might float through the Void forever. Atlantean Scions once traveled to these worlds easily via the Gods\u2019 voidbirds and an Axis Mundi made of stars; but when the pantheon decided to isolate itself from all others, many passages through the Void closed without explanation or warning. Scions wonder whether ending their civilization\u2019s self-imposed exile will open them again, or whether they\u2019re gone for good. </div> </div> </div>The MidRealms works much like the Mage realms (I don\u2019t remember the names in Awekaning) and the Void is the Astral space between the several realms.<br /> As I said, Heroes usually don\u2019t have much of power to deal with this kind of situation, but Demigods probably can navigate better in the void (like a powerful Mage would do) and gods have all the tools for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 08-25-2020, 08:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T05:22:42-07:00","id":1410271,"title":"","content":"I think Mage the Awakening take alot of inspiration from the early christian Gnostics as well as a few things written by Plato.<br /> (Or rather takes inspiration from other works that take inspiration from those sources).<br /> <br /> Im sure research on those subject could offer alot of material for a midrealm or terra incognita in scion.<br /> <br /> The issue ones need to be careful with (in addition to everything said by Sacerdos above) is not to try and interpret the cosmology of other culture with this.<br /> Like you shouldnt go &quot;Maya from Deva mythology is definitely the Astral space in mage&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T10:30:22-07:00","id":1410325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1410130-astral-space-in-scion?p=1410237#post1410237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wyrd if you want to play Mage, you can play Mage, you don't gotta come in here and go &amp;quot;Okay but how do I make Scion into Mage?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> I don't go into the WoD threads and piss and moan about the mythic inaccuracies of all of the various splats, because then I'd be the asshole and people would quite rightly go &amp;quot;Buddy fuck off and go back to Scion if you like Scion so much&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Edit: Some Cosmologies have Overworlds, and they're a thousand times more interesting than how I've heard these Astral Realms described. I recommend just using THOSE, because they'll inevitably make for a better story than trying to take something from a different game line and trying to beat it into shape to fit a different line, tone, and setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would note that whether you're talking about Mage: the Ascension or Mage: the Awakening, there are a number of conceptual parallels. For example, if I were combining Scion 1e with Awakening 1e, I'd probably say that Awakening's Supernal World and Scion's Overworld are the same thing; it's just that Awakening focuses on Watchtower Realms while Scion deals with Godrealms. Both Awakening and Scion have changed considerably since their respective first editions, so I'm not sure how this would work if trying to mesh their second editions; but I suspect parallels could be established. <br /> <br /> The Ascension parallel is in some ways more fundamental: Scion's \u201call myths are true\u201d concept is similar to Ascension's multifaceted reality, as demonstrated by the way that Motifs in Scion 2e serve a similar role to Practices in M20. More generally, the mythological constructs that Scion 2e calls Pantheons are very similar in concept to M20's concept of the Focus, or what earlier editions of Ascension called Paradigms. <br /> <br /> With all that in mind, I wouldn't necessarily have a problem adding an Astral Space to Scion. But I'd want to tie it to a Pantheon where the notion of dreams and mindscapes having a reality of their own is a thing. I don't think any of the traditional Pantheons fit the bill; instead, I'd consider this to be part of a Scion variant (similar to Dragon or Mythos) where Scion is adapted to represent the likes of Santa Claus, Paul Bunyan, and others of that sort: beings who, unlike gods, <i>do</i> derive from and are sustained by human imagination. <br /> <br /> If combined with Scion proper, this \u201cRealm of the imagination\u201d wouldn't be \u201cthe space between the Godrealms\u201d; it would effectively be \u201canother Godrealm\u201d unto itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T11:57:54-07:00","id":1410354,"title":"","content":"Origin's Aether (p. 37) is closest to an Astral for Scion. I recommend that you use it as it is written, or it could cause a lot of confusion. Oneiros and Temenos is even possible a cohesive adaptation, but Anima Mundi can be very confused when compared to Overworlds and Primordial worldbodies. I also recommend caution, Legend in the World is defined by human beliefs. Allowing to manipulate Temenos can be very overpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15464-raphatheascended","name":"RaphaTheAscended","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T12:30:04-07:00","id":1410363,"title":"","content":"This seems to be another thread that starts out, &quot;hey, I have an idea for a cool campaign&quot; that quickly becomes, &quot;no, you can't play it that way.&quot; This seems to happen a lot here - is there a reason why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T12:36:36-07:00","id":1410367,"title":"","content":"Hm,.<br /> I guess the best analogy i could make would be someone wanting to play Vampire the Requiem but wants to play DC actually from Krypton Superman.<br /> <br /> Theres a certain backdrop expectation i guess going into not just scions but all games.<br /> And then that naturally invite the criticism of &quot;Do you actually want to play X game (scion in this instance)&quot;<br /> <br /> But an aspect that i feel is always ignored in response to the criticism is that there are core elements that are totally applicable to scion.<br /> But instead i feels theres a very big response of &quot;but how could i not engage with mythology instead?&quot;<br /> Which is a bit baffling i guess for people going into scion specifically because of the very prevalent mythology aspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T12:48:16-07:00","id":1410370,"title":"","content":"Oh another analogy i could make (apologies for the double posting).<br /> <br /> Say you design a rpg based around how computer works (hardware and software).<br /> You make the decision to not go with movie hacking logic and instead ask help with engineers, programmers and mathematician to make the content of the game correlate to real life computers as much as possible.<br /> <br /> Now this game is gonna attract a certain group of people who find computers interesting.<br /> <br /> And then you get people also coming in because they want shadowrun type hacking and computers in the game.<br /> <br /> So you're gonna have a natural clash between people who find real world working of computers interesting and people who are more into pop culture approach to computer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T13:38:46-07:00","id":1410385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RaphaTheAscended</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1410130-astral-space-in-scion?p=1410354#post1410354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Origin's Aether (p. 37) is closest to an Astral for Scion. I recommend that you use it as it is written, or it could cause a lot of confusion. Oneiros and Temenos is even possible a cohesive adaptation, but Anima Mundi can be very confused when compared to Overworlds and Primordial worldbodies. I also recommend caution, Legend in the World is defined by human beliefs. Allowing to manipulate Temenos can be very overpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Scion's <i>Aether</i> Axis Mundi sounds as perfect fit - it even mention to be called Astral Plane, sometimes! For ease of discussion, I will quote <b>Origin</b> part on it:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Aether: Greek, Indian, and modern occult sources have written extensively about the Aether, and have given it other names, such as Indra\u2019s Net and the Astral<br /> Plane. The Aether is composed of the fifth, subtle element that creates space and distance. Platonists believe that it transmits the \u201clight\u201d of ideal objects which in turn, create the substance of other realms. Mortals have long used techniques to send their souls into the Aether, where they can rise to contemplate The World and Overworld, and Scions may use the same techniques. Ordeals in the Aether take the form of riddles, enigmas, and acts of deep self-realization, administered by the abstract beings who dwell there.<br /> Unfortunately, it\u2019s impossible to physically traverse the Aether except with the use of obscure magical powers, and exceedingly difficult to use it to travel to the Underworld. </div> </div> </div>It really sounds as direct reference of Oneiros and Temenos of <b>Mage</b>, 1:1 almost. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Now add only possiblity of travel by the other Axis Mundi from <i>Aether</i>, and we have already what I really need. ( For example, I need some way to cross to <i>Yggdrasil</i> - and all that is needed for me is there. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T13:38:53-07:00","id":1410386,"title":"","content":"The original supposition for Scion 1e was pretty simple in many ways, it was about playing Heroes, Demigods and Gods, and it was absolutely based on Greek mythology, there were other pantheons, we know that, but it was build (including the way the other pantheons worked in general) on a Greek mythology structure, with gods having children or adopting them from other gods, and Titans fighting against gods.<br /> <br /> It offended many people, most Hindu and modern religions, as the way it portraits their gods were simplistic and completely centered on the Greek paradigm of gods.<br /> <br /> Then the second edition came with the proposition of fixing the broken system AND the way the mythologies would be faced in the game.<br /> <br /> The problem, as I see, is, some people don\u2019t think Scion is Just a Game, as it deal with real beliefs it must be true to the beliefs, while most of the players see Scion as just another game that you can go from mortal to god, not different from Deities and Demigods from D&amp;D or The Primal Order (Old but gold, worth the money! Check it).<br /> <br /> Honestly, this conflict just throw people away from the game. I am here trying to spread the gospel (intended pun) of Scion, but it really gets hard to do if the community acts aggressively against the casual player.<br /> When people come to this forum asking for help or suggestions for a crossover, they are looking for people that know the game and played enough to help with the mechanics and conversions. If they ask any Scion mechanics question in any other forum I will not see, because I don\u2019t go around CoD or WoD forums often, and so will not be able to help.<br /> <br /> People like Watcher and Sacerdos (there are many others that know a lot, but they Are my \u201cMyth-source\u201d of choice), spread the ideas of how the several mythologies can be better portrayed in your game. And I do enjoy how many of the more \u201chardcore players\u201d value the theme of Scion, but when we get to a new player (and I include myself here) we don\u2019t need to know everything to play a game just because there is a lot to know.<br /> <br /> I, for example, like mithology, and Scion pushes me to look for more, but I just can\u2019t deal with all the information to play 5 different pantheons in the same game and still keep fidelity to any of them. I just want to have fun and tell a story about heroes becoming gods, or maybe how gods live in a world that don\u2019t give them value, or how heroes defeat monsters (and I really don\u2019t want to go back to D&amp;D for personal reasons).<br /> <br /> Well, that\u2019s it, hope nobody got offended as I called Scion \u201cjust a game\u201d...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 08-25-2020, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T15:00:07-07:00","id":1410405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1410130-astral-space-in-scion?p=1410386#post1410386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that\u2019s it, hope nobody got offended as I called Scion \u201cjust a game\u201d...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone would be offended at that, but, I think the important thing is to not use 'Just a Game' as a way to put down deeper criticisms of a text. I think the reason that the phrase sets a lot of people off is because it often is used to try to stifle debate or discussion, when something being a game doesn't diminish its importance or value. Be it a TTRPG, a video game, a movie, music, a novel, all of these things are texts that can be read and evaluated by the audience. Just because something is intended for entertainment doesn't give it a pass, or reduce its importance, or the potential dangers of these things perpetuating bad material.<br /> <br /> Scion is a game, and just like any piece of media I choose to pay for, I want it to be worth the money I pay for it. Additionally, I want to think about what I spend my money on. Scion being a game doesn't magically free it of responsibility for its contents, or diminish the value of us from reading critically into the information it gives us.<br /> <br /> I think ultimately people can do whatever they like with a piece of media, though there are some things I would consider tasteless (whitewashing characters, bi-erasure, etc) that people do when consuming texts. Scion is somewhat more of an interesting issue, as it is a mirror of real life faiths that deserve respect. I think the ultimate issue here in how people interpret things can be summed up in this idea of the mirror quite well. I am interested in the reflection (the myths, both in the factual material that can be found in the reflection, putting a critical eye at flaws in the reflection, and creating my own reflections and attempting to create the best reflections I can) where other people are interested in the mirror itself (the system, the mechanics, what the book tells you, the fictional structure put together to create the reflection). I find the mirror itself to be ultimately unimportant save for how it effects the reflection, while other people find the reflection to be unimportant save for how it expresses the function of the mirror. Both of these ways to approach Scion are fine as long as you are trying to be respectful, because it is the least we can do when enjoying these wonderful stories from various cultures.<br /> <br /> Now, I will also just add, I'm not actually a guy, though no worries or concern there about that. But also, while I doubt people are going to be offended that you called Scion a game, they will probably not be cool with you saying &quot;oriental&quot; which you might want to change as that is actually a not-cool word to use.<br /> <br /> On the topic of the idea of Astral Realms, I'm <i>pretty sure</i> that it is an actual religious concept from the last few centuries, so there should 100% be an Astral Realm in Scion. It is just that Pantheon's specific concept. This is a good example why I don't really find a need to add stuff to Scion outside of the base premise, there is probably a version of it that already exists in the setting somewhere. It is what I love about the game.<br /> <br /> P.S. I don't only hold Scion to these standards. It isn't unique in that regard at all. If it helps, I actually have <i>very serious</i> criticisms of Deities and Demigods and the Druid Class as well. Like, <i>massive</i>. I think the first publication of it is responsible for the largest reaching piece of misinformation regarding the Celts and Celtic religion in the last century that has caused such a high level of damage to the cultural conception of these things I think it will be <i>at least</i> a century until it can be resolved. The new Netflix series about Excalibur I critique for trying (badly) to write Welsh in Ogam, messing up both the Welsh and the Ogam. The television show Brittania (I think?) I can't stand because it perpetuates flat out super-bad depictions of Celtic peoples, drawing on the 'Noble Savage' and all that. Nothing is above critique, especially when dealing with history and the like. What makes Scion slightly unique is it makes a claim to history, there is a claim that the books are drawing on actual material which gives it a sense of legitimacy and people consume the texts and absorb the information. It markets itself with this idea of a faithful depiction of these texts, and they hire scholars to work on the projects, which gives people confidence in the information they are consuming because the product has presented itself as working with authorities and trying to 'get things right' which is great! Up until an entire chapter is 99.9% made up but frames itself only as partly fictional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 08-25-2020, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T15:25:07-07:00","id":1410413,"title":"","content":"I try to minimize what Scion represents to you or any of the other people here, and that way I tried to explain the situation as I see. Scion HAS a tremendous research and become a much more respectable work from several points of view, and I love how it made me go deeper on my personal quest for more information. But for many people looking for a new game to play, that would also be enthralled by the concepts of Scion, the first impact they have in the forum, is that the community is not receptive to new players and crossovers. That is it, Scion is a game with a tremendous potential of becoming more than just a game to many people (including me).<br /> <br /> As you suggested, I removes the disrespectful Words, and I am sorry about the guy thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T16:01:15-07:00","id":1410420,"title":"","content":"I'm not in favour of negative representations at all, and I think Scion has gone a long way toward being respectful of the faiths contained within. My concern is that many threads seem to focus on maintaining fully accurate depictions of gods and pantheons, while stifling any variation in the name of a good/fun game (read: enjoyable to participants while still maintaining at least basic respect to cultures and beliefs). &quot;Just a game&quot; means, to me, &quot;not a speech by a world leader&quot; and &quot;not a paper by a scholar&quot;; it won't change mass opinion or mislead nations, but should entertain the group within the genre you are playing. I don't get &quot;play Scion but hide the Gods&quot; or &quot;play Scion but feature Christianity/Islam instead&quot;, but those are choices for a Storyteller to make, not me. If you want to create your own Pantheons, or have those in the game change in the decades/centuries/millennia since they were actively worshipped by societies in the real world, you should feel you can, and feel you can discuss those ideas freely here, on the Scion forums.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T16:19:39-07:00","id":1410423,"title":"","content":"The Ascended Masters pantheon (based on New Age Theosophy) is a fanwork that may be dropping soon on the Storypath Nexus, that is likely to include things like the Astral Plane as an Axis Mundi (just my guess based on limited knowledge).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 08-26-2020, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T16:34:14-07:00","id":1410426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1410130-astral-space-in-scion?p=1410385#post1410385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, Scion's <i>Aether</i> Axis Mundi sounds as perfect fit - it even mention to be called Astral Plane, sometimes! For ease of discussion, I will quote <b>Origin</b> part on it:<br /> <br /> <br /> It really sounds as direct reference of Oneiros and Temenos of <b>Mage</b>, 1:1 almost. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Now add only possiblity of travel by the other Axis Mundi from <i>Aether</i>, and we have already what I really need. ( For example, I need some way to cross to <i>Yggdrasil</i> - and all that is needed for me is there. )</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is more a rules clarification for people who have drawing my attention to this. It's not a problem to transcribe bits from publications [within reason], like a few paragraphs.<br /> <br /> However, it's usually best to just summarize.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1410130-astral-space-in-scion?p=1410363#post1410363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems to be another thread that starts out, &quot;hey, I have an idea for a cool campaign&quot; that quickly becomes, &quot;no, you can't play it that way.&quot; This seems to happen a lot here - is there a reason why?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Don't editorialize on other posters. If you have a complaint there's the report button.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T18:28:58-07:00","id":1410433,"title":"","content":"With respect, I was asking a question, not intending to editorialize on any one person; there have been several threads where new (or old) players suggest ideas, and seem to be discouraged, and I was curious to know why. No finger-pointing intended, but also not a complaint about anyone specifically (hence the lack of reporting).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T19:44:11-07:00","id":1410438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1410130-astral-space-in-scion#post1410130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was great fan of <b>Mage: The Awakening</b>. In <b>Scion</b> I have most of what I loved about <b>MtAw</b> - powerful magic, mythological stories, otherworld realms - and with <b>Companion</b>, even Atlantis is here. In <b>MtAw </b>I loved also one more element - dream realms of Astral Space, connecting whole humanity. From my read of <b>Scion 2E Origin</b> and <b>Hero</b> I do not see realms as Astral - but maybe I missed something? If not, how do you think I could insert Astral in <b>Scion</b>? Common Otherworld for Gods and mythical beings, created by dreams of humans, that let some of mythics to enter it?<br /> <br /> EDIT: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15464-raphatheascended\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar15464_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"15464\" data-vbnamecard=\"15464\">RaphaTheAscended</a> found the solution - <i>Aether</i> Realm, from <b>Scion</b> 2E <b>Origin</b> book. Here is quote about it:</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the Astral was extremely cool as well. I never looked at it since first edition but there was some neat stuff there that you can change the way people thought and acted through influencing some of these bigger than one person dreams. That was great for the wars between the Pentacle and the Seers, you could literally change the way the world thinks (or just a single mind). I always thought that was suppose to be bigger part of what Mage was going to be about or maybe it was just one direction you could go with your campaign.<br /> <br /> I also liked how it progressed from personal dream space/soul --&gt; humanity's dreamspace --&gt; the dreamspace of nature --&gt; Abyss --&gt; the Supernal Realms. Kind of gave the hint that the Supernal realms are all within our souls.<br /> <br /> What exactly did you like about the Astral?<br /> <br /> My take is it is really, really tied to Mage's cosmology but if you wanted to make it in Scion that there is this shared dream state that you can use, go ahead. Which elements of the Astral did you want to use/like? I assume the Abyss would be out since that's not really a thing in Scion. Are you thinking of having the &quot;real&quot; gods go into the Astral and interact with the &quot;dream&quot; gods? If you don use you might want to have Fate interact more strongly in the symbolic word.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11830-joboo","name":"Joboo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T00:23:29-07:00","id":1410462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joboo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1410130-astral-space-in-scion?p=1410438#post1410438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also liked how it progressed from personal dream space/soul --&gt; humanity's dreamspace --&gt; the dreamspace of nature --&gt; Abyss --&gt; the Supernal Realms. Kind of gave the hint that the Supernal realms are all within our souls.<br /> <br /> What exactly did you like about the Astral?<br /> <br /> (...)<br /> Which elements of the Astral did you want to use/like? I assume the Abyss would be out since that's not really a thing in Scion. Are you thinking of having the &quot;real&quot; gods go into the Astral and interact with the &quot;dream&quot; gods? If you don use you might want to have Fate interact more strongly in the symbolic word.</div> </div> </div> </div>So whole Astral cosmology to humanity's dreamspace ( Temons ) surly, maybe natrue dreamscape ( Anima Mundi ) also.<br /> <br /> I think that in Scion, there would not be divide between 'real' gods and 'dream' gods - Dream gods would be just one of personifications of particular god. Just like you have material, living iIncarnations of them. However, I think that dream Incarnation can somehow be independent of general god multirealms status - so 'fight' over Astral's / Aether rule of dream one can be more profound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T14:24:12-07:00","id":1410566,"title":"","content":"It leads us to interesting problem - <b>What would be Dream Gods stats in Aether?</b> Would they simply work as Incarnations, made of 'dream stuff'? Limit to Legend 5 for them, to show they are much lesser things than proper gods?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-26-2020, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T21:55:11-07:00","id":1410612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1410130-astral-space-in-scion?p=1410566#post1410566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It leads us to interesting problem - <b>What would be Dream Gods stats in Aether?</b> Would they simply work as Incarnations, made of 'dream stuff'? Limit to Legend 5 for them, to show they are much lesser things than proper gods?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you may be making a mistake by trying to lump all gods and cosmologies under the same limitations. Like Hermes was considered to be responsible for delivering dreams to mortals, it just feels weird to declare that dreamspace is somehow uniquely special for Gods compared to all the other parts of the cosmologies that they have influence over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24666-ravian","name":"Ravian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T08:11:42-07:00","id":1410680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1410130-astral-space-in-scion?p=1410221#post1410221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Will watch it, but I suspect the Veil is like the Underworld in WoD / CoD - i.e. cross realm of dead from where they go to their proper afterlife realms?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Are not hindu Deva having their own Dream Domains, also? With reality being Maya and all that? Adding those two with Platonic Ideas realm of Theoi - and you have basis for Astral. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what Maya is... Maya is the force that causes the Manifest World to bind Beings within it. It does not refer to dream realms, but to the actual manifest reality all around you, as well as the entirety of the 14 Worlds of Existence... it is also not an illusion, but very real, simply not the core essence of Divinity. In at least one tradition, the purpose of Maya is to ensure that we can go about daily life instead of constantly lost in the joyful contemplation of Divinity, making it also not evil as a lot of pop culture tends to show it as.<br /> <br /> Your real best chance of an actual Astral Realm is from the Ascended Masters of Theosophy, which I believe someone was working on as a fan Pantheon... though obviously that would still be limited to their Cosmology alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T12:29:41-07:00","id":1410739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1410130-astral-space-in-scion?p=1410680#post1410680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not what Maya is... Maya is the force that causes the Manifest World to bind Beings within it. It does not refer to dream realms, but to the actual manifest reality all around you, as well as the entirety of the 14 Worlds of Existence... it is also not an illusion, but very real, simply not the core essence of Divinity. In at least one tradition, the purpose of Maya is to ensure that we can go about daily life instead of constantly lost in the joyful contemplation of Divinity, making it also not evil as a lot of pop culture tends to show it as.<br /> <br /> Your real best chance of an actual Astral Realm is from the Ascended Masters of Theosophy, which I believe someone was working on as a fan Pantheon... though obviously that would still be limited to their Cosmology alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of the problem is that Maya was used in to limited a way in early translations from Urdu/Hindi and now has independent meanings in English. All attempts at clarification simply make things murkier. At least on posting boards.<br /> <br /> Why not recommend a good book on the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T12:45:43-07:00","id":1410748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1410130-astral-space-in-scion?p=1410739#post1410739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Part of the problem is that Maya was used in to limited a way in early translations from Urdu/Hindi and now has independent meanings in English. All attempts at clarification simply make things murkier. At least on posting boards.<br /> <br /> Why not recommend a good book on the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>... Are you trying to explain the concept of Maya to someone who is a practitioner of a form of Hinduism?<br /> <br /> Edit: Like, I'm sure that Samudra could recommend a passage that explains what Maya truly is but-","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T13:09:43-07:00","id":1410752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1410130-astral-space-in-scion?p=1410748#post1410748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... Are you trying to explain the concept of Maya to someone who is a practitioner of a form of Hinduism?<br /> <br /> Edit: Like, I'm sure that Samudra could recommend a passage that explains what Maya truly is but-</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I am suggesting that the liguistic history of the word Maya in English may be walling off his truer and clearer perspective from communication.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T14:21:38-07:00","id":1410762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1410130-astral-space-in-scion?p=1410612#post1410612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you may be making a mistake by trying to lump all gods and cosmologies under the same limitations. Like Hermes was considered to be responsible for delivering dreams to mortals, it just feels weird to declare that dreamspace is somehow uniquely special for Gods compared to all the other parts of the cosmologies that they have influence over.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I do not stated that. I meant that each God has material <b>and</b> dream version ( and probably other Realms versions ) - being various Incarnations. Those Gods with preview related to Dreams would have slightly stronger their Dream Incarnations - but <b>all </b>Gods still will be somewhere in the Aether ( Scion canonical 'Astral Realm' ). Hermes, Apollo and Ares all have their own Dream versions - but Hermes being God of Messenger have slightly more powerful version in the Aether than other twos. This kind of things...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-28-2020, 03:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T16:57:24-07:00","id":1410781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1410130-astral-space-in-scion?p=1410752#post1410752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I am suggesting that the liguistic history of the word Maya in English may be walling off his truer and clearer perspective from communication.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Let's move from on this conversation point.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T03:16:11-07:00","id":1410817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1410130-astral-space-in-scion?p=1410762#post1410762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I do not stated that. I meant that each God has material <b>and</b> dream version ( and probably other Realms versions ) - being various Incarnations. Those Gods with preview related to Dreams would have slightly stronger their Dream Incarnations - but <b>all </b>Gods still will be somewhere in the Aether ( Scion canonical 'Astral Realm' ). Hermes, Apollo and Ares all have their own Dream versions - but Hermes being God of Messenger have slightly more powerful version in the Aether than other twos. This kind of things...</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea conceptually. I don't think there needs to be a specific split between &quot;material&quot; forms and &quot;dream&quot; forms, any more than there needs to be a specific meditation form or mind-wandering-in-the-middle-of-class form. Rather, the gods just slough off incarnations or mantles or such like as they want/need. It makes sense to me that those gods with more stake in dreams would be more likely to appear in those forms, but not that they find it any easier or harder than others in their pantheon. I do enjoy the thought of Hades asking Hypnos to pop a message along to his Scion, but just as easily deciding to manifest himself in/as a dream, either overtly or as some symbol-laden dream vision. And with the roiling mass of probability distributions that mythoreality in The World is, both scenerios could just as well be the same thing.<br /> <br /> Engaging with the mechanics then, I would argue that it makes sense that a &quot;dream form&quot; incarnation would be limited in Legend, but for no reason more than the same reason gods don't appear on terra firma in their full Legendary splendour. A high Legend incarnation, dream or not, is gonna leave big ol' eddies of Fate in their wake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26056-cassiecataria","name":"CassieCataria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26056_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}